  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Yes, I am aware this sounds like a crazy thing to do.\nSuppose we want an animation that tilts our entire armature. For example, placing our avatar on a spinning platform whilst AFK.\nThis can be solved via a rotation or aim constraint on the armature.\nDoing this is totally fine in Desktop. But in VR, this causes very strange behaviour. Even with the constraint disabled, bending down causes your view point to enter your chest. Moving backwards and forwards desyncs your avatar from your head location. Your IK generally is not solved correctly.\nThis is a pretty nasty bug and it'd be helpful to be told if this is fixable, or is a \"won't fix\" limitation with VRC's player animation system.",
